Backport of upstream NUT commit ce2364e2b1e79406248be50b01a031db67c1c9fd
("drivers: preserve libusb context across USB reopens (richcomm only)").
No CVE was assigned, so this patch has no VEX entry and no SBOM-fragment
analysis entry.

richcomm_usb is one of the three USB drivers in this build that do not go
through the shared libusb-1.0 layer: it calls libusb_init(NULL) from its
own usb_device_open() and libusb_exit(NULL) from its own
usb_device_close(), so patches/libusb-exit-reconnect-deadlock.patch, which
fixes drivers/libusb1.c, does not reach it. Every reopen therefore drives
the default context's refcount to zero and waits on libusb's internal
synchronization for URBs that a device reset or an unexpected disconnect
orphaned and that never drain — the same teardown deadlock, in this
driver's own copy of the misuse.

The fix has the same shape as the shared-path one: initialize the context
once on the first open behind a file-scope flag, stop calling libusb_exit
from the close path, and release it exactly once at driver cleanup. There
is no atexit handler and no SIGALRM bound here, unlike the shared-path
backport: upstream released the context from upsdrv_cleanup() instead, and
this patch is upstream verbatim.

bcmxcp_usb and nutdrv_atcl_usb carry the same misuse in their own code and
are unfixed upstream, so no hunks are authored for them here.

Only the drivers/richcomm_usb.c hunks of the upstream commit are included,
which is the whole commit; it touched no other file.

Remove this patch when NUT_VERSION moves to v2.8.6+, which ships the fix.
See CONTRIBUTING ("Upstream sources may carry checked-in patches") for the
removal checklist.

diff --git a/drivers/richcomm_usb.c b/drivers/richcomm_usb.c
index c20e1b6ea2..ad03c9dec5 100644
--- a/drivers/richcomm_usb.c
+++ b/drivers/richcomm_usb.c
@@ -68,6 +68,9 @@ static usb_device_id_t richcomm_usb_id[] = {
 static usb_dev_handle	*udev = NULL;
 static USBDevice_t	usbdevice;
 static unsigned int	comm_failures = 0;
+#if WITH_LIBUSB_1_0
+static int		libusb_inited = 0;
+#endif
 
 /* Forward decls */
 static int instcmd(const char *cmdname, const char *extra);
@@ -305,7 +308,6 @@ static int usb_device_close(usb_dev_handle *handle)
 
 #if WITH_LIBUSB_1_0
 		libusb_close(handle);
-		libusb_exit(NULL);
 #else
 		ret = usb_close(handle);
 #endif
@@ -332,9 +334,11 @@ static int usb_device_open(usb_dev_handle **handlep, USBDevice_t *device, USBDev
 
 	/* libusb base init */
 #if WITH_LIBUSB_1_0
-	if (libusb_init(NULL) < 0) {
-		libusb_exit(NULL);
-		fatal_with_errno(EXIT_FAILURE, "Failed to init libusb 1.0");
+	if (!libusb_inited) {
+		if (libusb_init(NULL) < 0) {
+			fatal_with_errno(EXIT_FAILURE, "Failed to init libusb 1.0");
+		}
+		libusb_inited = 1;
 	}
 #else  /* => WITH_LIBUSB_0_1 */
 	usb_init();
@@ -636,6 +640,13 @@ void upsdrv_cleanup(void)
 	free(usbdevice.Product);
 	free(usbdevice.Serial);
 	free(usbdevice.Bus);
+
+#if WITH_LIBUSB_1_0
+	if (libusb_inited) {
+		libusb_exit(NULL);
+		libusb_inited = 0;
+	}
+#endif
 }
 
 void upsdrv_initinfo(void)
